{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "urn:hsvg:2.0:schema:capability:physics",
  "title": "HyperSVG 2.0 capability physics: Physics",
  "description": "the settings addons.physics of a block (D28): bodies, at most 32, each a drawn part, component or compound that has translate ranges on both axes; a body owns the whole transform of its target | bodies are circles (radius) or boxes (width and height, axis aligned); units are drawing coordinates, seconds and degrees, y points down; the centre of a body is origin + its translation; origin and position default to [0, 0] | fixed 120 Hz steps on the owner's clock, every step a clock advance covers (no catch-up cap); semi-implicit Euler with one inverse-mass impulse and correction pass over body pairs, taken in ascending id order; the same configuration, seed and commands give the same motion on one JavaScript engine | mass 0 makes a static body (a wall: it cannot be thrown or kicked); otherwise mass is 0.001..1000 (default 1); gravity defaults to [0, 600]; bounce defaults to 0.35 (a pair uses the lower value); friction defaults to 2 and is exponential velocity drag, in flight too; floor is a y coordinate in the shared space and respects the body's extent | bodies start asleep and wake on a throw, a kick or a moving peer; a body sleeps after 24 quiet ticks (speed below 0.1 and displacement below 0.01) | events physics:hit:<body> and physics:landed:<body> carry {other}: another body id, floor, x:min, x:max, y:min or y:max; contacts fire on entry, never while resting; landed means downward support under positive y gravity; physics:rest:<body> fires once when the body sleeps; contacts lists the others a body reports (omitted: all) | gravity, bounce, friction and rest are numbers or formulas proven inside their ranges; configuration is sampled at mount and at each throw or kick, and never changes a flight in progress | the call physics.throw with {body, vx, vy} sets the body's velocity (drawing units per second) and, with x and y, its translation first; physics.kick with {body, vx, vy} adds to the body's current velocity; body is a formula, usually a quoted body id ('ball'); the others are numbers or numeric formulas | a drag control named under controls with releaseVelocity true adds velocity [vx, vy] to the payload of its event and missEvent when released: drawing units per second, measured over the last 100 ms of pointer movement, 0 when the pointer was still | keyboard throw: for such a drag picked up by keyboard (Enter or Space), each arrow key press adds keyVelocityStep (default 400) drawing units per second to the pending velocity in that direction (y points down); Enter or Space releases with it, Escape cancels; each component is clamped to +-10000 | reduced motion: the simulation runs unchanged and its events fire at their normal times; the drawing shows each body at its rest position",
  "$comment": "Generated by docs/spec-2.0-work/tools/schema/make-schemas.mjs from the spec/2.0 machine files. Do not edit.",
